  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-7064" textLabel="short-chain acyl-CoA oxidase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-7064" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="130" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>|FRAME: TAX-3702| has six acyl-CoA oxidase (ACX) genes. &lt;i&gt;In vitro&lt;/i&gt; enzyme assays have determined substrate specificities for |FRAME: AT4G16760| (long chain), |FRAME: AT5G65110| (very-long chain), |FRAME: AT1G06290| (medium chain) and |FRAME: AT3G51840| (short chain). &lt;i&gt;In vivo&lt;/i&gt; studies of enzyme activities using each ACX mutants confirmed &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; results |CITS: [15743450]|. The product of the |FRAME: AT3G51840| gene was shown to oxidize |FRAME: PROPIONYL-COA| and |FRAME: 4-HYDROXY-BUTYRYL-COA| with similar efficiency |CITS: [27856910]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-7064" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT3G51840-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-25447, RXN-25445, RXN-19386, RXN-12583" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005777" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="4" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="10212254" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-PEROXISOME-PL" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightExp" value="180." />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="180." />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15743450" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_27856910" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-9180" textLabel="propanoyl-CoA oxidase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-9180" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="130" width="140" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">The |FRAME: AT3G51840 ACX4| gene of |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col| encodes a |FRAME: CPLX-7064 short-chain acyl-CoA oxidase| |CITS: [15743450]|. The enzyme has similar activities with |FRAME: PROPIONYL-COA propanoyl-CoA| and |FRAME: 4-HYDROXY-BUTYRYL-COA 4-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA|. The enzyme was recruited to participate in the synthetic carbon dioxide fixation pathway named CETCH cycle as a propanoyl-CoA oxidase. However, since |FRAME: 4-HYDROXY-BUTYRYL-COA 4-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA| is also an intermediate in the cycle, the second activity was undesired. In order to solve this problem, the gene was modified to generate a T134L mutation. The mutation lowered the activity of the enzyme with |FRAME: 4-HYDROXY-BUTYRYL-COA 4-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA| by two orders of magnitude, while the reaction with |FRAME: PROPIONYL-COA propanoyl-CoA| was only affected by a factor of ten. The engineered enzyme was named Pco (for propanoyl-CoA oxidase) |CITS: [27856910]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-9180" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="MONOMER-20106" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="1" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-25453" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="4" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15743450" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_27856910" />
    </Group>
